.TH "FWD CONFIG RM" "1" "2026-08-12" "fwdit" "fwd config rm Manual"
.SH NAME
fwd\-config\-rm \- Remove a configuration value at one scope, revealing
the next-higher-precedence value.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fwd config rm
[OPTIONS] {key}
.SH DESCRIPTION
Remove a configuration value at one scope, revealing the
next-higher-precedence value.
.PP
Missing values are reported as a successful no-op. Interactive removal
confirms; agents and pipes must pass
--force. Omitting --user, --project, and --target selects user scope.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-user\fP
Remove the user-wide value from ~/.fwd/config.toml; this is the default scope.
.TP
\fB\-\-project\fP
Remove only the current project's value.
.TP
\fB\-t,\fP \-\-target <str>
Remove one target-specific value without changing the target itself.
.TP
\fB\-f,\fP \-\-force
Skip confirmation; required in non-interactive mode when the value exists.
.SH EXIT STATUS
\fB0\fP indicates success. Any nonzero value indicates an error.
.SH REPORTING BUGS
Report issues at \fIhttps://github.com/Sid-MB/fwd/issues\fP.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBfwd\fP(1)
